SEG = 'HAN'
CAT = 'ftasHandling'
Q = [
    ("Under s 3 of the Firearms Act 1996 (Tas), possession of a firearm includes:",
     "Custody or control", ["Legal ownership only", "Registration", "Physical carrying only"],
     "Section 3 says possession includes custody or control, so a firearm in your car or shed can be in your possession even if you are not holding it."),
    ("Besides firing it, the Act's definition of use of a firearm includes:",
     "Holding it as if to fire", ["Only pulling its trigger", "Cleaning it at home", "Carrying it in a case"],
     "Section 3 defines use as firing the firearm or holding it so as to cause a reasonable belief that it will be fired, whether or not it can be fired."),
    ("A rifle with its bolt removed and a blocked barrel is, under s 3:",
     "Still a firearm", ["A firearm part only", "No longer a firearm", "An imitation firearm"],
     "Section 3 counts as a firearm anything that would be one if it did not have something missing from it or a defect or obstruction in it."),
    ("Which item is ammunition under Tasmanian law?",
     "Airgun pellets", ["Empty brass cases", "Cleaning patches", "Lead fishing sinkers"],
     "Section 3 defines ammunition to include cartridges, primed cases with charge and projectile, blankfire cartridges, airgun pellets, training and gas cartridges, explosive components and paintball pellets."),
    ("In the Code's list of functions, cocking a firearm means:",
     "Compressing the mainspring", ["Closing the breech fully", "Pulling the trigger back", "Pushing a round into the chamber"],
     "The Code defines cocking as compressing the firing pin main spring and engaging the firing pin to the trigger mechanism."),
    ("How is a break-open shotgun usually loaded?",
     "By hand into the barrels", ["From a tubular magazine", "From a detachable box magazine", "Down the muzzle with a rod"],
     "The Code says cartridges are fed into the barrels of a break-open shotgun by hand before the barrels are closed and the action locks."),
    ("To open a fired break-open shotgun, the Code says you move the:",
     "Locking lever", ["Fore-end forward", "Bolt handle up", "Hammer back"],
     "The Code says the locking lever is moved, usually to the right, letting the action break open so the cartridges can be removed."),
    ("A bolt-action rifle locks when the bolt is pushed forward and:",
     "Turned down", ["Pulled back", "Lifted up", "Removed fully"],
     "The Code says the round is fed and the action locked when the bolt is pushed forward and the bolt handle turned down; lifting it unlocks the action."),
    ("The Code's name for a magazine-fed rifle whose bolt is worked by hand is a:",
     "Bolt-action repeater", ["Self-loading rifle", "Break-open express rifle", "Trombone-action rifle"],
     "The Code says bolt actions may be single shot or fitted with a magazine, when they may be called bolt-action repeaters."),
    ("Which item do the Firearms Regulations 2026 prescribe as ammunition?",
     "Seal control cap", ["Bird scaring kite", "Fishing flare", "Rope launcher"],
     "Regulation 9 prescribes a seal control cap, a powder-loaded projectile with a percussion cap that bursts apart on impact, as ammunition."),
    ("For a revolver, s 3 measures barrel length from the:",
     "Muzzle to front of cylinder", ["Muzzle to the rear sight", "Muzzle to the hammer spur", "Front sight to the grip"],
     "Section 3 measures a revolver's barrel from the muzzle to the breech end just in front of the cylinder; for other firearms, from the muzzle to the breech face."),
    ("Which of these counts as a firearm under s 3 of the Tasmanian Act?",
     "Blankfire firearm", ["Captive bolt device", "Nail gun", "Unmodified foam blaster"],
     "Section 3 includes a blankfire firearm in the definition of firearm. The Firearms Regulations 2026 declare unmodified captive bolt devices, nail guns and foam blasters not to be firearms."),
    ("Under s 110, a firearm can be unsafe because of a mechanical defect or:",
     "Its general condition", ["Its age in years", "Its calibre or gauge", "Its colour or finish"],
     "Section 110(3) treats a firearm as unsafe if, because of a mechanical defect or its general condition, or for any other reason, it may reasonably be considered unsafe."),
    ("A doctor treats a patient for a wound they suspect a firearm caused. Under s 158A, the doctor must:",
     "Report it to police", ["Treat it privately", "Tell only the family", "Note it in the file"],
     "Section 158A requires a medical practitioner who suspects a firearm wound to report to a police officer as soon as practicable and to keep any recovered ammunition fragments for police."),
    ("To possess an inherited heirloom firearm that cannot be fired, a Tasmanian needs:",
     "A firearm heirlooms licence", ["A permit to acquire only", "No licence at all", "A firearms museum licence"],
     "Section 13 bars possessing an heirloom firearm without a firearm heirlooms licence, and s 47 requires it to be rendered permanently incapable of being fired in the prescribed way."),
    ("Which tool seats the projectile in a muzzle-loading firearm?",
     "Ramrod", ["Cleaning patch", "Choke key", "Bolt handle"],
     "The Code says a measure of powder goes in and the projectile is seated with a ramrod."),
    ("Which part of a cartridge sets off the propellant powder?",
     "Primer", ["Projectile", "Wad", "Crimp"],
     "The Code lists a cartridge's parts as the projectile, propellant powder, cartridge case and primer; the struck primer ignites the powder."),
    ("Which shotgun sizes does the Code name as the most popular?",
     "12, 20 and .410", ["10, 16 and 28 gauge", "28 gauge and .410", "8, 10 and 16 gauge"],
     "The Code says the most popular break-open shotguns are 12 and 20 gauge and .410 calibre."),
    ("The Code says air rifles must be treated with the same care as any firearm because they:",
     "Can cause serious injury", ["Need a Category B licence", "Use real cartridges", "Cannot be unloaded"],
     "The Code warns that an air rifle is capable of causing serious injury and is not a toy, even though it is propelled by compressed air or gas."),
    ("Loaded cartridges are in a break-open shotgun and its barrels are closed. The Code says it is now:",
     "Locked and ready to fire", ["Safe until cocked by hand", "Unable to fire yet", "Only partly loaded"],
     "The Code says that once the barrels are closed the action locks and the shotgun is loaded and ready to fire, so extreme caution is needed at this time."),
]
